Task: Replace date-derived FY with explicit selection (Phase 1, Tier 1)
Track: fy_tax_pack_20260729

SUMMARY
The tax report now takes its financial year from an explicit selection
rather than inferring it from today's date.

FILES
- lib/tax/fy.ts - added resolveFyEndYear
- tests/lib/tax/fy.test.ts - 7 new tests (29 total)
- components/financial-year-select.tsx (new) - client Select writing ?fy=
- app/(dashboard)/properties/[propertyId]/tax-report/page.tsx - accepts
  searchParams, uses fyBounds/selectableFyEndYears/resolveFyEndYear,
  resolves stamp duty, renders the selector beside the breadcrumb
- components/tax-report-pdf.tsx - TaxReportData gains stampDuty
  {amount, source}; exported stampDutyLabelFor
- components/tax-report.tsx - reads the resolved stamp duty

DEFECTS FIXED
1. Wrong year. The derivation returned the IN-PROGRESS financial year. On
   29 July 2026 it produced 2026-27; a 2026 return needs 2025-26. There
   was no way to request a past year at all.
2. Timezone drift. Bounds were built with new Date(y, m, d) (local) then
   serialised via toISOString(). At UTC+10 the start became 30 June
   instead of 1 July, pulling a day of the prior year's expenses in.
3. Divergent stamp duty. tax-report.tsx read property.stamp_duty while
   tax-report-pdf.tsx read roiInputs.stamp_duty, so the screen and the
   PDF could show different CGT cost bases for the same property. Now
   resolved once server-side: recorded purchase cost first, ROI planning
   input as a labelled fallback, "(not recorded)" when absent.

DESIGN NOTES
- Only completed years are offered. A partial year cannot produce a
  meaningful tax report, and offering it is what made the wrong year easy
  to pick.
- An unrecognised ?fy= falls back to the newest year rather than 404ing,
  so a stale link still renders something correct.
- Query-parameter resolution was extracted into resolveFyEndYear so it is
  pure and testable rather than inline page logic.
- Open-ended tenancies clamp to the year end rather than today.
  Equivalent for completed years, and removes the date dependence.

